      // auto-displayed by Android's system tray whenever the app is backgrounded/killed, which
      // SKIPS onMessageReceived in MyFirebaseMessagingService.kt entirely (that only fires for
      // data-only messages, or while the app is in the foreground). Since the whole point of that
      // custom service is to guarantee every message gets its own notification, the payload must
      // stay data-only so it's actually invoked in the background/killed case that matters most.
      // convKey/msg* let an open chat screen paint the incoming bubble straight from the push,
      // instead of waiting for the next poll to see it in (eventually consistent) storage.
